<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 97,162 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 97,162 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 97,162 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 57,353 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   June 10</p>
<p>    Export cargo		16,747	26,202</p>
<p>    Import cargo		80,415	31,151</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 New Tatina		11/6</p>
<p>Palm oil	     10,000	 Wawasan Courage	 Due</p>
<p>High speed diesel  56,000	 Al-Maqwa		  Due</p>
<p>Palm oil		9,300	 Vi Vi		     12/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		4,000	 United Tina	     13/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
